  ],
  "slug": "gene-expression-5e8d",
  "summary": "Unified computational frameworks now span multi-omics translation, perturbation screens, and chromatin readouts across recent preprints and publications.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational frameworks that combine multiple data modalities, models, or learned representations to infer regulatory and epigenomic states. scTranslation benchmarks translation between single-cell multi-omics modalities, and TopOmics applies topic modelling across any combination of omics types with benchmarks against existing methods. Ensemble strategies recur: fourSynergy weights existing 4C-seq interaction callers by gradient-free optimization, and the enhancer-promoter framework integrates multi-cell-line features with an XGBoost meta-classifier. Deep models target chromatin and methylation directly, with THC-net predicting A/B compartments from six histone modifications and MethyNano using supervised contrastive pretraining for nanopore 5mC detection. Brieflow adds an end-to-end pipeline for optical pooled screening data. What is new is the emphasis on multimodal integration within unified, benchmarked frameworks, although the items remain methodologically heterogeneous.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-06-03"
}
